## Stage 5: Database Design & Architecture
Understanding how underlying relational databases store and manage structure.
* **Data Modeling:** Entity-Relationship (ER) Diagrams, One-to-One, One-to-Many, and Many-to-Many relationships
* **Normalization:** 1NF, 2NF, 3NF, and BCNF to minimize data redundancy
* **Denormalization:** When and why to break normalization rules for analytical workloads (e.g., Star Schema, Snowflake Schema)
* **ACID Properties:** Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, Durability in transactions
* **Transactions & Concurrency:** BEGIN TRANSACTION, Isolation levels (READ COMMITTED, SERIALIZABLE), Deadlocks
